WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:32.871
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:33.141 --> 00:34.172
[This drama is fiction.]

3
00:34.172 --> 00:36.328
[Characters, places, events, organization, and the setting have no connection to reality.]

4
00:36.328 --> 00:38.256
[Child actors were filmed under safe conditions.]

5
00:47.332 --> 00:49.065
Attorney Park Tae Su.

6
00:54.117 --> 00:55.517
Eun Kyung?

7
00:59.054 --> 01:00.454
Eun Kyung.

8
01:05.921 --> 01:07.537
Don't you remember me?

9
01:08.173 --> 01:09.573
Do you know me?

10
01:11.156 --> 01:13.512
Well, It's been a while.

11
01:13.512 --> 01:16.372
But you could've at least recognized me.

12
01:18.809 --> 01:21.587
I'll come back later, Attorney Park.

13
01:35.283 --> 01:37.312
Maybe we can talk tomorrow, then.

14
01:48.644 --> 01:51.841
You haven't changed, Cha Eun Kyung.

15
01:57.031 --> 01:59.466
[Episode 2]

16
02:08.562 --> 02:11.200
What are you doing here?

17
02:11.200 --> 02:14.495
Didn't Jae Hee say she wanted to stay a few more nights to spend time with you?

18
02:15.824 --> 02:18.436
Didn't you tell her to stay so you could get more work done?

19
02:19.286 --> 02:21.663
You haven't changed at all. Work always comes first.

20
02:21.663 --> 02:23.367
Don't assume things.

21
02:24.207 --> 02:28.441
And visitation is part of our agreement, so please stick to the schedule.

22
02:29.981 --> 02:32.645
Well, at least Jae Hee has Ji Yoon.

23
02:32.645 --> 02:35.308
They went from friends to sisters. How nice is that?

24
02:36.717 --> 02:41.408
Jae Hee has finally gotten used to you getting remarried.

25
02:43.685 --> 02:45.085
Don't tell me you got any problem.

26
02:47.564 --> 02:49.540
What are you talking about?

27
02:49.540 --> 02:51.876
I'm here over a medical malpractice suit.

28
02:56.073 --> 02:57.473
Bye.

29
03:26.103 --> 03:27.372
Hello.

30
03:27.372 --> 03:29.738
- I'll head in first. - Okay.

31
03:32.442 --> 03:36.181
I thought I should explain, so I came by unannounced.

32
03:36.181 --> 03:39.491
Oh, Jae Hee explained to me. It's fine.

33
03:39.491 --> 03:41.592
I knew we had an agreement,

34
03:41.592 --> 03:44.246
but Jae Hee wanted to stay longer. I'm sorry.

35
03:44.246 --> 03:47.916
Her dad had to leave for work early today, so I came to drop her off.

36
03:47.916 --> 03:49.584
It's fine.

37
03:50.585 --> 03:53.547
Is everything okay with you?

38
03:53.547 --> 03:55.139
Yes, I'm good, thank you.

39
03:58.349 --> 03:59.783
Yoo Hee!

40
04:01.972 --> 04:03.991
Thank you for the dumplings.

41
04:03.991 --> 04:07.118
I heard you made those yourself. Thank you so much.

42
04:07.118 --> 04:09.760
My pleasure. We should both look out for the kids.

43
04:27.185 --> 04:29.541
Why did Yoo Hee drop you off?

44
04:29.541 --> 04:31.541
Is Dad busy these days?

45
04:31.541 --> 04:32.625
Yeah.

46
04:32.625 --> 04:34.795
There's some trouble at Dad's hospital.

47
04:35.922 --> 04:38.216
I'm here over a medical malpractice suit.

48
04:38.216 --> 04:39.559
Why are you asking?

49
04:39.559 --> 04:41.179
Nothing.

50
04:41.179 --> 04:43.025
How's the new math academy?

51
04:44.032 --> 04:46.018
I love it.

52
04:46.018 --> 04:47.059
That's good.

53
04:47.059 --> 04:48.939
Actually, I want to study somewhere else.

54
04:48.939 --> 04:50.979
The kid next to me at the library is so loud.

55
04:53.130 --> 04:56.735
Then how about I set up a study area for you at home?

56
04:56.735 --> 04:58.424
- Sounds good. - Okay.

57
05:08.851 --> 05:11.069
- See you later. - Yeah.

58
05:11.069 --> 05:12.469
See you later!

59
05:19.799 --> 05:21.219
The library?

60
05:48.745 --> 05:50.736
Could you keep it down, please?

61
05:50.736 --> 05:52.586
[Law School Library]

62
05:53.583 --> 05:57.812
If it's bothering you so much, why don't you study at home?

63
06:03.802 --> 06:05.887
He's still the same, huh?

64
06:05.887 --> 06:07.633
So annoying.

65
06:13.937 --> 06:15.126
Hey, Kang.

66
06:15.126 --> 06:18.567
How's the councilor's debt collection going?

67
06:18.567 --> 06:20.771
Visit the councilor regularly and keep him updated.

68
06:24.455 --> 06:26.693
Sir, I'm a lawyer.

69
06:26.693 --> 06:30.164
You can't keep sending me out for consultations like this.

70
06:30.164 --> 06:32.434
That's outdated. We can't do business like this--

71
06:32.434 --> 06:35.208
Are you telling me how to run my business?

72
06:35.208 --> 06:37.058
Hey Kang, are you ignoring me?

73
06:37.058 --> 06:41.184
Think you're big enough to talk back to me? Then pick one.

74
06:41.184 --> 06:45.336
- Excuse me? - Do what I say, or quit!

75
07:02.279 --> 07:05.608
You're Tae Su from By the Law, right?

76
07:05.608 --> 07:07.908
Wow, you're so handsome!

77
07:07.908 --> 07:12.079
I watch all your videos! I really love them!

78
07:12.079 --> 07:13.479
Thank you.

79
07:17.668 --> 07:20.120
Good morning, Attorney Cha.

80
07:23.346 --> 07:26.501
You've got a minute? We need to talk.

81
07:27.393 --> 07:28.793
About what?

82
07:36.061 --> 07:37.701
After you, Ma'am.

83
07:52.169 --> 07:54.569
Canned coffee again?

84
08:02.546 --> 08:06.307
We're both going through a hard time, so let's try to coexist.

85
08:13.581 --> 08:14.981
You remember!

86
08:16.059 --> 08:17.926
As you saw earlier,

87
08:17.926 --> 08:21.273
I'm just as famous as you are now.

88
08:21.273 --> 08:24.313
Use honorifics with me, Attorney Park.

89
08:29.698 --> 08:32.528
All right, Attorney Cha.

90
08:32.528 --> 08:36.497
I've got two things to discuss. First...

91
08:37.205 --> 08:40.968
Why was that client here yesterday?

92
08:40.968 --> 08:43.082
Was it a medical malpractice case?

93
08:43.082 --> 08:45.937
That's a bit out of line, don't you think?

94
08:45.937 --> 08:48.830
A lawyer's duty of confidentiality!

95
08:50.410 --> 08:51.932
And the second one?

96
08:53.721 --> 08:55.298
Name your price.

97
08:55.298 --> 08:57.893
How much to get you off the eighth floor?

98
08:57.893 --> 09:01.117
I'll pay handsomely. Please leave.

99
09:01.117 --> 09:03.190
Now that's pretty out of line.

100
09:04.232 --> 09:07.181
What'll it take to get you out?

101
09:07.181 --> 09:09.159
I want the seventh floor, too.

102
09:09.780 --> 09:14.143
Go ahead and try. Everyone will still see this place as part of REBOM.

103
09:14.143 --> 09:16.744
I've been here for over two years.

104
09:16.744 --> 09:20.290
Then from now on, everyone will know this place as TAESU.

105
09:20.290 --> 09:22.481
I'm going to stay here for 20 years.

106
09:22.481 --> 09:24.363
Then I guess we're done.

107
09:34.090 --> 09:35.946
[Congratulations, Cha Eun Kyung! Top Scorer on the 46th Bar Exam in Record Time]

108
09:39.142 --> 09:41.088
I passed early, thanks to you.

109
09:42.896 --> 09:44.532
You were so noisy, I couldn't stand it.

110
09:45.499 --> 09:46.899
Bye.

111
09:51.936 --> 09:55.602
Still the same. You say your piece and just walk away.

112
09:59.579 --> 10:03.684
You'll see. You'll be the one leaving.

113
10:03.684 --> 10:05.064
[Attorney Jeon Eun Ho]

114
10:09.255 --> 10:13.343
Hello, this is Attorney Jeon. We spoke last week.

115
10:14.594 --> 10:17.984
Oh, I see... You signed with another firm.

116
10:19.766 --> 10:22.728
TAESU Law Firm?

117
10:22.728 --> 10:25.795
All right. Thank you.

118
10:32.946 --> 10:35.540
It's annoying. Really annoying.

119
10:39.436 --> 10:41.207
[TAESU Law Firm, Senior Partner Park Tae Su]

120
10:45.291 --> 10:46.627
[Your Strongest Sword and Shield]

121
11:21.570 --> 11:24.873
Ma'am, do you know Attorney Park?

122
11:24.873 --> 11:28.334
We went to college together. He's such a copycat.

123
11:28.334 --> 11:31.245
When he was studying for the bar, he even got the same pen and notebook as me.

124
11:31.245 --> 11:35.938
So the guy paying double rent for the eighth floor is Attorney Park,

125
11:35.938 --> 11:39.373
and you two went to the same college?

126
11:39.373 --> 11:42.079
Wow, Small world!

127
11:45.933 --> 11:51.483
Ma'am, Attorney Park only got a little attention because the algorithm picked him.

128
11:51.483 --> 11:53.985
But you're the one clients pick.

129
11:53.985 --> 11:59.198
Beautiful, smart, a real professional lawyer. Got it?

130
11:59.198 --> 12:01.362
Very convincing. You're a lawyer, after all.

131
12:01.362 --> 12:02.389
Thank you.

132
12:02.389 --> 12:05.896
Let's see how long he lasts.

133
12:05.896 --> 12:08.499
With rent this high, paying double is ridiculous.

134
12:08.499 --> 12:11.038
I know. It's like a war in here.

135
12:11.038 --> 12:15.578
But if we're going to strengthen our forces in this war,

136
12:15.578 --> 12:20.721
I think we need another lawyer. What do you think?

137
12:20.721 --> 12:23.700
- I was just about to tell you. - Yes.

138
12:23.700 --> 12:26.843
- I think I found one. - No way! No way!

139
12:26.843 --> 12:29.814
You said a new hire was coming, but no one ever showed up.

140
12:29.814 --> 12:31.427
I'm pretty sure this time.

141
12:32.249 --> 12:33.649
Who is it?

142
12:37.519 --> 12:39.224
Kang Hye Seong.

143
12:39.224 --> 12:40.401
What?

144
12:40.401 --> 12:41.741
She never gives up.

145
12:41.741 --> 12:46.121
She fights to the end for what's best for her clients.

146
12:46.121 --> 12:48.165
I haven't seen a lawyer like that in ages.

147
12:48.165 --> 12:51.710
- I told you that when we were having lunch. - Exactly!

148
12:51.710 --> 12:56.965
I'll find out if she's interested in divorce cases and open to switching firms.

149
12:56.965 --> 12:58.585
Need to find the right timing.

150
13:00.676 --> 13:03.674
[Case 02: Timing] Should I call her first?

151
13:10.285 --> 13:12.510
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm's Problem Solver, Attorney Kang Hye Seong]

152
13:21.571 --> 13:24.785
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm] Councilor, did you see Attorney Kang sing?

153
13:24.785 --> 13:26.620
- I'm sorry. - What the...

154
13:26.620 --> 13:32.360
She's good at everything. Drinking, civil cases, criminal cases, you name it.

155
13:32.360 --> 13:34.955
Don't worry.

156
13:34.955 --> 13:38.377
She's a nobody. She has to do whatever I tell her.

157
13:38.377 --> 13:41.506
Then I'll see you tonight. Thank you.

158
13:41.506 --> 13:42.690
Yes.

159
13:44.761 --> 13:46.727
What is this, the '80s?

160
13:49.267 --> 13:52.712
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm]

161
14:00.611 --> 14:03.573
Can I meet Attorney Kang?

162
14:03.573 --> 14:06.300
Her schedule is completely booked today.

163
14:06.300 --> 14:09.547
If you don't have an appointment, you'll have to wait in line.

164
14:11.719 --> 14:13.119
Okay.

165
14:36.440 --> 14:39.484
There's an empty seat. Would you like to move?

166
14:39.484 --> 14:41.412
- Sure. - Yes.

167
15:05.636 --> 15:09.869
Does she really handle all these consultations by herself?

168
15:10.474 --> 15:12.976
I'm here for a consultation.

169
15:12.976 --> 15:15.441
Please have a seat and wait a moment.

170
15:23.903 --> 15:26.846
Could you give this to Attorney Kang?

171
15:26.846 --> 15:29.246
- Please ask her to call me. - Sure.

172
15:35.373 --> 15:37.912
She's really busy. You can't just--

173
15:37.912 --> 15:39.237
[Senior Partner Cha Eun Kyung]

174
15:42.831 --> 15:45.018
Cha Eun Kyung...

175
15:49.390 --> 15:53.220
We've been married for five years, and we don't have kids.

176
15:54.101 --> 15:55.983
Please help me get a divorce.

177
15:55.983 --> 15:57.956
What's the reason?

178
15:58.939 --> 16:00.725
He goes gambling.

179
16:10.677 --> 16:12.452
[Cheonghae Zone Game Center The best odds in town!]

180
16:12.452 --> 16:17.909
He took about 500 million won from his father and lost it.

181
16:19.918 --> 16:22.948
I told you! One more time, and I'm divorcing you!

182
16:25.196 --> 16:29.529
When I told him to stop gambling, he hit me.

183
16:33.930 --> 16:36.935
I said I wouldn't do it!

184
16:36.935 --> 16:38.575
I said I wouldn't!

185
16:44.484 --> 16:46.320
Get over here.

186
16:46.320 --> 16:47.800
Get over here!

187
16:53.452 --> 16:56.925
- Stop it! - Stay still!

188
16:56.925 --> 16:59.159
Just stay still!

189
17:00.693 --> 17:04.414
There. That's better.

190
17:14.608 --> 17:19.603
Every time I brought up divorce, he'd sign a written promise not to do it again.

191
17:19.603 --> 17:21.896
And then it happened all over again.

192
17:21.896 --> 17:23.553
[Emergency Room]

193
17:23.553 --> 17:28.719
He only signed it because his parents would disinherit him if we divorced.

194
17:30.989 --> 17:35.859
But there were more than gambling and abuse.

195
17:39.623 --> 17:41.229
There was another woman?

196
17:42.644 --> 17:44.872
Another woman would be better.

197
17:45.629 --> 17:49.257
Gosh, I've been waiting forever.

198
17:49.257 --> 17:50.567
Was he having an affair with a man?

199
17:50.567 --> 17:52.260
You weren't waiting for me.

200
17:52.260 --> 17:54.601
You were waiting for this, right?

201
17:54.601 --> 17:57.342
You are the best!

202
18:02.479 --> 18:03.879
Drugs.

203
18:09.735 --> 18:12.311
Gambling, abuse, and drugs...

204
18:12.311 --> 18:15.070
That's more than enough grounds for divorce.

205
18:15.070 --> 18:16.841
What do you want to do?

206
18:21.569 --> 18:25.711
I want to make him pay. As much as possible.

207
18:25.711 --> 18:30.169
Why just make him pay? We should crush him completely!

208
18:30.169 --> 18:31.569
How?

209
18:35.293 --> 18:40.394
"Criminal Charges," "Property Division," "Property Seizure," and "Restraining Order."

210
18:41.101 --> 18:43.680
Let's file all four at once.

211
18:44.771 --> 18:46.647
Should we start with the Criminal complaint?

212
18:46.647 --> 18:48.998
We can't file a criminal complaint yet.

213
18:48.998 --> 18:51.815
For now, let's just file for divorce mediation.

214
18:51.815 --> 18:55.636
Why? We should go after property division and file criminal charges, too!

215
18:55.636 --> 18:58.982
The attorney upstairs told me to file all four.

216
19:03.414 --> 19:08.221
Most of your husband's three billion won in assets was gifted to him.

217
19:08.221 --> 19:11.682
You've only been married for five years and have no kids.

218
19:11.682 --> 19:14.376
You probably won't get much in the property division.

219
19:19.765 --> 19:25.123
He has three billion won, and his parents have tens of billions.

220
19:25.123 --> 19:27.149
Because of him, I've...

221
19:28.732 --> 19:34.071
had to take antidepressants, and I can't live a normal life. But he is...

222
19:34.071 --> 19:37.188
That's why we shouldn't sue right now.

223
19:37.188 --> 19:40.548
His parents are wealthy, not your husband.

224
19:40.548 --> 19:43.569
If his assets are deemed separate property, splitting them won't be easy.

225
19:43.569 --> 19:45.633
And compensation won't be much.

226
19:45.633 --> 19:49.231
You may not understand what I'm saying right now.

227
19:49.231 --> 19:52.246
But if you want some compensation for what you've been through,

228
19:52.246 --> 19:56.301
mediation is a better option than going to trial.

229
19:56.301 --> 19:59.476
Just watch how I handle this.

230
20:20.609 --> 20:22.936
[Hyeseong's Bunsik]

231
20:24.207 --> 20:27.329
Do what I say, or quit!

232
20:27.329 --> 20:31.080
But I know everyone in Gwangjin. Do you really think you can practice law here?

233
20:31.080 --> 20:33.956
Besides, because of your dad, you're stuck in Gwangjin anyway, right?

234
20:42.347 --> 20:44.308
Dad!

235
20:44.308 --> 20:46.109
Hey, sweetie. You're home.

236
20:46.109 --> 20:47.509
Let me carry that.

237
21:10.713 --> 21:14.199
Dad, should I sell tteokbokki with you?

238
21:15.005 --> 21:16.405
What?

239
21:17.549 --> 21:20.677
Don't be ridiculous.

240
21:20.677 --> 21:22.261
Who knows?

241
21:22.261 --> 21:26.069
I might make more money than I do as a lawyer.

242
21:26.069 --> 21:29.402
Besides, AI's going to replace knowledge workers soon anyway.

243
21:30.519 --> 21:33.111
Making more money isn't what matters.

244
21:33.111 --> 21:34.653
Of course it is.

245
21:34.653 --> 21:39.445
You worked so hard paying off my law school loans.

246
21:39.445 --> 21:41.631
Don't make money your priority.

247
21:41.631 --> 21:44.651
You wanted to be a lawyer so badly.

248
21:49.056 --> 21:54.413
Dad, do you know why I wanted to become a lawyer in the first place?

249
21:55.504 --> 21:58.020
Don't tell me it was to make a lot of money.

250
21:58.020 --> 22:00.388
Gosh, you're impossible!

251
22:09.835 --> 22:12.243
Did the surgery go well?

252
22:12.243 --> 22:18.199
[Five years ago] Yes, but I'm not sure he can walk again.

253
22:18.199 --> 22:20.639
[Operating Room] He needs help from his family.

254
22:30.593 --> 22:33.042
[Congratulations on joining DAEJEONG Law Firm]

255
22:41.174 --> 22:43.734
- Are you okay? - Yeah, I'm fine.

256
22:50.060 --> 22:53.684
All right. We'll look for another attorney then.

257
22:53.684 --> 22:57.373
Hope your father makes a full recovery.

258
22:58.897 --> 23:02.655
Dad, you must be sick of hospital food. I'll make you something nice.

259
23:26.515 --> 23:27.915
Yes.

260
23:29.354 --> 23:34.372
Ma'am, you went all the way to Gwangjin yourself? I could've gone.

261
23:34.372 --> 23:36.090
I wanted to talk to her in person.

262
23:36.090 --> 23:38.951
What did Attorney Kang say? Can she move?

263
23:38.951 --> 23:41.818
Is she a fan of yours? Can she start right away?

264
23:41.818 --> 23:43.152
I didn't get to meet her.

265
23:43.152 --> 23:45.665
You went all that way and didn't meet her?

266
23:47.322 --> 23:49.366
There were so many people waiting for consultations.

267
23:49.366 --> 23:52.076
The firm had no specialty and handled a high volume of cases for low fees.

268
23:52.076 --> 23:55.048
It was more like a public service desk than a law firm.

269
23:55.956 --> 23:58.459
And the senior partner seems awful.

270
23:58.459 --> 24:01.516
It might be a perfect time to recruit her, but...

271
24:01.516 --> 24:03.773
The timing does seem right,

272
24:03.773 --> 24:06.550
but she'd have to give up her entire career in civil and criminal law

273
24:06.550 --> 24:08.820
and start from scratch in divorce law.

274
24:08.820 --> 24:10.820
That's what worries you, right?

275
24:10.820 --> 24:13.383
Exactly! You catch on fast.

276
24:14.683 --> 24:20.157
Criminal Case No. 201-5423 is now in session.

277
24:20.157 --> 24:22.862
Prosecution, please state the charges.

278
24:23.984 --> 24:27.478
On March 3, 2026, at around 8 p.m.,

279
24:27.478 --> 24:30.445
The defendant entered her ex-boyfriend's home without permission by entering the door code.

280
24:30.445 --> 24:34.804
She trespassed into his home, disturbing his peace and privacy.

281
24:34.804 --> 24:40.077
Therefore, the defendant violated Article 319, Paragraph 1 of the Criminal Act.

282
24:40.077 --> 24:42.344
Defense, go ahead.

283
24:46.009 --> 24:48.415
I plead not guilty.

284
24:50.513 --> 24:54.195
- She looks like a rookie, pleading not guilty? - Your Honor.

285
24:54.195 --> 25:00.062
To prove trespassing, you must show that she intended to disturb the peace of his home.

286
25:00.062 --> 25:06.275
But my client wasn't trespassing. She was just trying to win back her ex.

287
25:06.275 --> 25:12.441
How can someone be an intruder after eight years of coming and going freely?

288
25:12.441 --> 25:16.045
The defendant made a terrible mistake, and what she did was wrong.

289
25:16.045 --> 25:19.287
But under the Criminal Act, she's not guilty!

290
25:20.167 --> 25:22.767
Oh, she's pretty good.

291
25:44.844 --> 25:47.254
Thank you for trusting REBOM with your case.

292
25:47.254 --> 25:51.457
But why do lawyers give such different advice?

293
25:52.114 --> 25:54.427
Well, everyone sees things differently.

294
25:54.427 --> 25:59.663
A judge's ruling and a lawyer's advice won't always be the same.

295
25:59.663 --> 26:01.297
Just trust me.

296
26:01.297 --> 26:02.981
Hello. Good morning.

297
26:02.981 --> 26:05.465
Good morning.

298
26:07.411 --> 26:08.856
Attorney Kang,

299
26:09.820 --> 26:13.845
I couldn't tell you yesterday with the senior partner around, but guess what?

300
26:14.798 --> 26:17.335
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung stopped by.

301
26:19.781 --> 26:21.484
Why?

302
26:21.484 --> 26:24.309
Maybe she came to recruit you.

303
26:25.831 --> 26:27.850
[REBOM Law Firm Senior Partner Cha Eun Kyung]

304
26:30.704 --> 26:31.737
[Central Family Court]

305
26:31.737 --> 26:34.984
The petition doesn't go into much detail.

306
26:34.984 --> 26:37.029
What's your reason for divorce?

307
26:37.029 --> 26:40.261
[Plaintiff's Table] Well, the reason is... d...

308
26:45.626 --> 26:48.129
Let's just say... deep emotional distress.

309
26:48.129 --> 26:51.196
[Defendant's Table] Yes.

310
26:51.196 --> 26:56.075
Respondent has approximately three billion won in assets. Is that correct?

311
26:56.075 --> 27:00.443
That's right. But most of his assets were gifted from his parents.

312
27:00.443 --> 27:02.459
They're not subject to division.

313
27:02.459 --> 27:04.474
Okay, but we're here for mediation, so...

314
27:04.474 --> 27:08.546
How much would you be willing to pay the applicant in a divorce?

315
27:08.546 --> 27:10.736
Well, as a goodwill gesture...

316
27:10.736 --> 27:13.743
He'd be willing to pay around 20 million won.

317
27:14.361 --> 27:16.288
20 million? You've got to be kidding me.

318
27:17.532 --> 27:21.048
We haven't taken any other legal action

319
27:21.048 --> 27:23.749
because we wanted to settle things amicably as a goodwill gesture.

320
27:23.749 --> 27:27.241
But it seems we have very different ideas about what a goodwill gesture means.

321
27:28.074 --> 27:30.170
20 million won is the most we can offer.

322
27:30.170 --> 27:31.723
Let's just settle for 20 million won.

323
27:31.723 --> 27:33.845
Then let's take it to court.

324
27:33.845 --> 27:35.252
Fine.

325
27:35.252 --> 27:39.265
- Maybe you should hear their offer-- - There's nothing to hear!

326
27:39.265 --> 27:41.719
Let's go to trial!

327
27:50.969 --> 27:52.798
Attorney Cha!

328
27:53.808 --> 27:55.901
Please wait over there.

329
27:59.088 --> 28:01.118
You're blackmailing us, not negotiating.

330
28:01.118 --> 28:03.383
It's not blackmail. It's a deal.

331
28:03.383 --> 28:05.038
That's what we do.

332
28:05.038 --> 28:07.985
Each side gives a little to find common ground.

333
28:07.985 --> 28:12.112
Are you saying you'll file criminal charges if we can't reach a settlement?

334
28:14.304 --> 28:16.234
Are you going to report him for using drugs?

335
28:16.234 --> 28:18.479
You got my point.

336
28:18.479 --> 28:23.875
Assault, rape, and drug use. All three charges.

337
28:23.875 --> 28:27.858
How can we trust that you won't file charges if we settle?

338
28:27.858 --> 28:31.134
Believe us or not, that's your problem.

339
28:31.134 --> 28:34.735
Put the house he's living in in her name, and we'll drop the whole thing.

340
28:34.735 --> 28:36.556
We'll even sign a confidentiality agreement.

341
28:36.556 --> 28:37.895
Have you lost your mind?

342
28:37.895 --> 28:40.617
That house is worth two billion won!

343
28:40.617 --> 28:44.039
How can a housewife who sits around all day get a house worth two billion won?

344
28:44.039 --> 28:47.826
Even lawyers who've worked 20 years can't afford a house like that these days!

345
28:47.826 --> 28:49.752
You still haven't bought one?

346
28:49.752 --> 28:52.870
Then maybe you should stay home, too.

347
28:52.870 --> 28:55.987
That's my final offer. Think it over and call me.

348
28:58.635 --> 29:02.398
Attorney Cha, I've been thinking...

349
29:03.392 --> 29:06.192
I'd be fine with just 180 million won.

350
29:07.004 --> 29:11.736
180 million? How'd you come up with that?

351
29:11.736 --> 29:17.195
3 million a month, 12 months a year, for 5 years.

352
29:17.195 --> 29:19.906
Just sign the divorce papers, please.

353
29:19.906 --> 29:22.060
- Please... - Get off me!

354
29:24.536 --> 29:29.628
I don't need money. Just please let me go!

355
29:30.852 --> 29:32.059
Hey.

356
29:32.059 --> 29:34.931
Do you know how much it costs to hire a housekeeper?

357
29:34.931 --> 29:38.710
I should pay at least three million won a month. Am I crazy?

358
29:40.135 --> 29:42.415
Shut up and clean my house.

359
29:43.055 --> 29:46.350
He treated me like his housekeeper,

360
29:46.350 --> 29:48.470
so I want at least that much.

361
29:50.729 --> 29:53.231
Then you're doing the math wrong.

362
29:54.523 --> 29:55.582
What?

363
29:55.582 --> 29:59.029
Abuse, assault, rape, drugs...

364
29:59.029 --> 30:01.657
You'll be scarred for life.

365
30:01.657 --> 30:05.232
You're only counting what you've done so far. What about compensation for

366
30:05.232 --> 30:07.183
the emotional damage you'll suffer in the future?

367
30:07.810 --> 30:10.989
2 billion won is worth fighting for. Don't back down.

368
30:11.667 --> 30:16.419
But if he pays, we'll let everything he's done go.

369
30:16.419 --> 30:20.527
You're getting a lot of money in exchange for keeping his big secret.

370
30:20.527 --> 30:22.985
You understand that's the deal, right?

371
30:26.765 --> 30:28.246
Yes.

372
30:40.718 --> 30:44.366
The defendant made a terrible mistake, and what she did was wrong.

373
30:44.366 --> 30:47.631
But under the Criminal Act, she's not guilty!

374
30:53.710 --> 30:55.363
[Gwangjin District Court: Case Number]

375
30:57.442 --> 30:58.827
[Case Search]

376
30:58.827 --> 31:01.133
[Verdict: Not Guilty, April 19, 2026]

377
31:01.133 --> 31:02.533
Not guilty?

378
31:04.124 --> 31:06.179
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm, Attorney: Kang Hye Seong] What?

379
31:06.179 --> 31:08.179
She really made it?

380
31:16.320 --> 31:18.481
[REBOM Law Firm: Interview Schedule]

381
31:23.546 --> 31:27.856
Hello. Please come this way.

382
31:27.856 --> 31:29.988
[REBOM Law Firm]

383
31:36.418 --> 31:39.328
Hello. Are you Attorney Kang Hye Seong?

384
31:39.328 --> 31:41.036
Right this way, please.

385
31:53.780 --> 31:57.689
- You're here? - Hello, Attorney Cha. Nice to see you again.

386
31:57.689 --> 31:59.089
Have a seat.

387
32:02.069 --> 32:05.866
You know we're a divorce law firm, right?

388
32:05.866 --> 32:07.807
Yes, I do.

389
32:08.617 --> 32:12.260
Any questions about us before we begin?

390
32:14.102 --> 32:18.041
May I ask why you decided to interview me?

391
32:19.084 --> 32:21.401
Whether you believed your client or not,

392
32:21.401 --> 32:25.548
you stood by your client and defended them to the very end.

393
32:25.548 --> 32:27.555
Your Honor, the agreement never says

394
32:27.555 --> 32:32.480
the plaintiff threatened or coerced her to meet other men.

395
32:32.480 --> 32:35.892
And you went out of your way to find evidence and bring it to court.

396
32:35.892 --> 32:39.175
These are market price reports for the condo from ten realtors.

397
32:39.175 --> 32:42.233
That's the kind of sincerity and dedication I was looking for.

398
32:44.152 --> 32:47.260
But I still lost the case.

399
32:48.323 --> 32:54.048
It's rare to find a lawyer who truly believes in their client and fights for them these days.

400
32:55.246 --> 32:57.218
Thank you.

401
32:57.218 --> 33:02.797
But to be honest, I have very little experience with divorce cases.

402
33:02.797 --> 33:05.130
I thought I could handle them,

403
33:05.130 --> 33:07.790
but they're very different from civil and criminal cases.

404
33:07.790 --> 33:09.886
Is she here to turn down the offer?

405
33:09.886 --> 33:11.847
That's right.

406
33:11.847 --> 33:18.026
Divorce cases are different. It's like...

407
33:18.026 --> 33:20.685
It's like an art in itself.

408
33:26.817 --> 33:31.979
If you join us, I'll offer you the highest salary for someone at your level.

409
33:33.035 --> 33:36.298
Do you need some time to think it over?

410
33:37.956 --> 33:41.043
Yes. Thank you for the offer.

411
33:41.043 --> 33:43.187
I'll think it over.

412
33:52.144 --> 33:53.843
Attorney Kang?

413
33:56.193 --> 33:59.934
Oh, you know me? I'm a subscriber to By the Law!

414
33:59.934 --> 34:01.436
Really?

415
34:01.436 --> 34:04.292
I was just about to become a fan of yours, too.

416
34:04.292 --> 34:07.819
- Sorry? - I saw you plead not guilty in court.

417
34:07.819 --> 34:09.915
And you actually got your client acquitted.

418
34:10.653 --> 34:13.413
An acquittal just five years into your career. That's impressive!

419
34:13.413 --> 34:17.231
You really do know me. Thank you.

420
34:17.996 --> 34:20.088
What brings you here?

421
34:20.088 --> 34:24.234
I'm here for an interview. Attorney Cha Eun Kyung invited me.

422
34:26.310 --> 34:28.924
[TAESU Law Firm, REBOM Law Firm] You're fast, Cha Eun Kyung.

423
34:28.924 --> 34:32.197
So she's worth hiring, even from Gwangjin?

424
34:33.258 --> 34:36.431
Since you're in Seoul, how about having tea?

425
34:36.431 --> 34:39.845
I'd like to chat with one of my subscribers.

426
34:41.406 --> 34:46.024
[TAESU Law Firm]

427
34:46.024 --> 34:48.366
I already know you're good in court.

428
34:49.129 --> 34:51.446
Have you brought in clients yourself?

429
34:51.446 --> 34:54.255
Yes! Our firm is small,

430
34:54.255 --> 34:57.256
so I handle consultations, take on cases, go to court,

431
34:57.256 --> 34:59.815
and even collect success fees all by myself.

432
35:01.857 --> 35:03.257
What do you specialize in?

433
35:04.354 --> 35:06.418
That's not common in small cities.

434
35:06.418 --> 35:09.630
I've handled civil, criminal, administrative, and divorce cases.

435
35:09.630 --> 35:13.844
I've handled a lot of small claims cases in particular.

436
35:13.844 --> 35:16.388
You're literally good at everything, huh?

437
35:16.388 --> 35:20.334
Then you must get a lot of bonuses.

438
35:21.209 --> 35:24.354
No, I just get a salary.

439
35:24.354 --> 35:28.482
Our firm is small, so even though we have a lot of cases, we don't make much.

440
35:28.482 --> 35:29.897
That's ridiculous!

441
35:29.897 --> 35:32.146
Why bring in clients if they're not paying you more?

442
35:32.146 --> 35:33.815
Just to make the senior partner richer?

443
35:34.906 --> 35:36.957
I wanted to learn along the way.

444
35:36.957 --> 35:40.710
I thought that would help me move on to the next step in my career.

445
35:46.219 --> 35:51.164
Then how about making TAESU your next step?

446
35:51.880 --> 35:56.087
I'll offer you a better deal than Attorney Cha did.

447
35:56.087 --> 35:57.487
Excuse me?

448
35:59.640 --> 36:02.690
We handle just about every kind of case.

449
36:02.690 --> 36:05.103
You seem like a criminal lawyer to me.

450
36:05.103 --> 36:09.983
You can't just throw away five years of experience in civil and criminal law.

451
36:11.401 --> 36:14.234
Thank you for the offer, but...

452
36:16.198 --> 36:19.567
Timing is everything!

453
36:36.463 --> 36:38.190
Hello, Ma'am.

454
36:39.822 --> 36:41.640
You're here, Ma'am.

455
36:41.640 --> 36:44.964
Should I reach out to Attorney Kang for you?

456
36:46.684 --> 36:49.625
She said she has some personal issues to deal with.

457
36:49.625 --> 36:51.425
Give her some time.

458
36:51.425 --> 36:52.825
- Yes. - Okay.

459
37:02.554 --> 37:04.067
Hey, Kang!

460
37:06.204 --> 37:07.572
There you are!

461
37:07.572 --> 37:11.195
One of my friends in Seoul told me something strange.

462
37:11.195 --> 37:13.752
Why did you meet Cha Eun Kyung when the trial was already over?

463
37:15.088 --> 37:16.134
- Why? - Well...

464
37:16.134 --> 37:18.823
To get you to join her firm? Right?

465
37:21.380 --> 37:27.000
- Yes, but I... - Think you'll make it in Seoul like she did?

466
37:28.393 --> 37:32.489
Without me, you're only half as good a lawyer. You're just handling routine cases.

467
37:32.489 --> 37:33.532
Got it?

468
37:36.848 --> 37:40.023
What? You want to hit me?

469
37:40.023 --> 37:44.086
You're just using your dad as an excuse not to go to Seoul, aren't you?

470
37:44.086 --> 37:48.489
You really think your dad can afford to open a firm for you just by selling tteokbokki?

471
37:48.489 --> 37:51.556
Oh, please. Know your place.

472
37:54.652 --> 38:00.057
I've recorded everything you've said to me, including today.

473
38:00.057 --> 38:03.117
I'll consider how to use this as a lawyer.

474
38:05.086 --> 38:07.971
Are you threatening me? Is that what I taught you?

475
38:07.971 --> 38:10.618
Did you ever teach me anything?

476
38:11.853 --> 38:13.659
I'm quitting.

477
38:13.659 --> 38:15.525
Send my things to me.

478
38:15.525 --> 38:16.818
Hey!

479
38:16.818 --> 38:19.151
Hey, Kang!

480
38:20.322 --> 38:22.604
Hey! I'm not finished yet!

481
38:41.445 --> 38:43.480
[Attorney Park Tae Su]

482
38:48.651 --> 38:50.516
Hello, Attorney Park.

483
38:50.516 --> 38:54.157
Attorney Kang, have you made up your mind?

484
38:54.157 --> 38:56.510
You've kept me waiting so long.

485
38:59.447 --> 39:03.197
Attorney Park, can we meet tomorrow?

486
39:03.197 --> 39:04.810
Sure!

487
39:06.393 --> 39:07.673
Yes.

488
39:10.664 --> 39:15.079
I knew she couldn't turn down my offer!

489
39:17.657 --> 39:22.342
Attorney Cha, I'm getting really worried. They still haven't called me.

490
39:22.342 --> 39:24.928
It's all about timing when it comes to settlement.

491
39:24.928 --> 39:27.264
Just wait a bit more.

492
39:27.264 --> 39:30.789
Should I call the police right now?

493
39:30.789 --> 39:34.702
If I don't report him, someone else could get hurt.

494
39:34.702 --> 39:39.484
Are you considering the public interest while you're getting divorced?

495
39:39.484 --> 39:42.446
Just think about what's best for you.

496
39:42.446 --> 39:47.671
He'll probably start getting nervous and offering more money by now.

497
39:48.271 --> 39:52.449
And make sure you leave the house. It's dangerous.

498
39:54.061 --> 39:55.375
So...

499
39:55.375 --> 39:59.796
I told you to raise the offer to around 100 million won!

500
39:59.796 --> 40:02.090
100 million? They're asking for two billion won!

501
40:02.090 --> 40:06.226
They won't even take that seriously. Let's just go to trial!

502
40:08.930 --> 40:12.863
So you're telling me to save my money and just go to prison?

503
40:12.863 --> 40:17.605
I'm telling you to pick one. Pay more or go to prison!

504
40:19.858 --> 40:21.408
Hello? Hel--

505
40:22.294 --> 40:26.104
What is wrong with him?

506
40:29.344 --> 40:30.824
What the...

507
40:32.537 --> 40:36.353
So you've decided? When can you start?

508
40:38.137 --> 40:42.167
Before I decide, I'd like to ask one thing.

509
40:43.563 --> 40:47.205
What role do you expect me to take on at the firm?

510
40:48.679 --> 40:54.466
She wants to know where she fits in? That means she wants to be useful.

511
40:54.466 --> 40:56.572
Oh, I want her even more.

512
40:58.814 --> 41:03.346
You have plenty of experience in both civil and criminal cases.

513
41:03.346 --> 41:06.826
I can put you on any team you prefer,

514
41:07.606 --> 41:12.631
but to sell the "Attorney Kang Gets Acquittals" image, the criminal team is a better fit.

515
41:19.582 --> 41:22.278
I'm sorry I can't give you an answer right away.

516
41:22.278 --> 41:26.297
Once I choose a firm, I tend to stay for a long time.

517
41:26.297 --> 41:28.157
Playing hard to get, huh?

518
41:28.868 --> 41:31.101
So I'm the one being interviewed now?

519
41:32.500 --> 41:34.573
Not at all!

520
41:34.573 --> 41:38.112
I can give you more time.

521
41:38.112 --> 41:40.166
Thank you.

522
41:53.124 --> 41:54.767
[REBOM Law Firm]

523
41:58.669 --> 42:02.048
[Attorney Cha Eun Kyung]

524
42:06.136 --> 42:07.860
[Boss]

525
42:09.788 --> 42:12.179
Hey! Are you seriously not coming to work?

526
42:12.179 --> 42:15.465
If you keep doing this, I'll sue you for breach of your employment contract

527
42:15.465 --> 42:18.602
and make sure no other firm hires you.

528
42:18.602 --> 42:21.295
Breach of my employment contract?

529
42:21.295 --> 42:24.358
I've asked you for years to give me a written contract, but you never did.

530
42:24.358 --> 42:27.225
Hey, Kang! Have you lost your mind?

531
42:41.122 --> 42:43.970
Hello, Attorney Kim Sang Chun, head of CHUNJEONG Law Firm.

532
42:43.970 --> 42:47.570
- This is Cha Eun Kyung. - How did she even get his name?

533
42:47.570 --> 42:49.463
Article 17 of the Labor Standards Act.

534
42:49.463 --> 42:54.341
You know that not providing a written contract is a criminal offense, right?

535
42:54.341 --> 42:57.579
How can you still not use written employment contracts these days?

536
42:57.579 --> 43:00.780
And stop calling Attorney Kang "hey."

537
43:00.780 --> 43:03.522
Isn't that a breach of an attorney's duty to maintain dignity?

538
43:03.522 --> 43:09.245
Who are you to tell me what to do? Are you her boss already?

539
43:09.245 --> 43:13.525
Well, I'm just her senior lawyer.

540
43:14.226 --> 43:15.819
For now.

541
43:19.860 --> 43:22.339
Hello? Hello!

542
43:23.542 --> 43:25.006
Unbelievable!

543
43:26.481 --> 43:29.426
Thank you, Attorney Cha.

544
43:29.426 --> 43:32.936
What brings you here? Did you come to see me?

545
43:32.936 --> 43:37.782
No... I came to meet Attorney Park.

546
43:37.782 --> 43:39.435
Park Tae Su again?

547
43:40.041 --> 43:42.929
Did I miss my chance?

548
43:44.148 --> 43:46.463
No. Not yet.

549
43:48.650 --> 43:53.456
We don't send our lawyers out for consultations.

550
43:53.456 --> 43:55.533
And we don't pressure them to bring in clients.

551
43:56.196 --> 44:00.445
- How did you find all that out? - I'm Cha Eun Kyung.

552
44:00.445 --> 44:01.845
I looked into everything.

553
44:04.199 --> 44:06.736
I've been waiting for you, Kang.

554
44:09.413 --> 44:14.155
Your passion and sincerity toward your clients.

555
44:14.155 --> 44:17.541
Those matter more in the divorce team than in other departments.

556
44:18.305 --> 44:21.444
I think you'd make a great divorce lawyer.

557
44:22.306 --> 44:25.639
Me? You really think so?

558
44:25.639 --> 44:27.146
Of course I do.

559
44:29.232 --> 44:34.763
Actually, there's something I've wanted to ask you.

560
44:34.763 --> 44:38.698
Go ahead. I'm not opposing counsel anymore.

561
44:38.698 --> 44:44.177
In the Seo Ji Hoon and Park Na Yeon case, Park said she didn't want a divorce back then.

562
44:44.177 --> 44:46.723
How did you convince your client?

563
44:47.876 --> 44:50.051
I showed her what was in store for her.

564
44:51.797 --> 44:54.576
If you want to learn those things, come be my associate.

565
44:55.509 --> 44:59.466
So I can hire you now, Attorney Kang?

566
45:03.225 --> 45:05.825
Yes, if the offer still stands.

567
45:20.005 --> 45:21.751
I'm home.

568
45:21.751 --> 45:23.745
Hey, sweetheart. You're home!

569
45:29.871 --> 45:31.271
Dad.

570
45:32.129 --> 45:33.529
I...

571
45:34.423 --> 45:36.801
I'm thinking of moving to a firm in Seoul.

572
45:36.801 --> 45:38.201
Really?

573
45:39.303 --> 45:43.939
Wow! That's great! What made you decide?

574
45:43.939 --> 45:46.230
I met someone I want to learn from.

575
45:49.445 --> 45:51.845
So, here's the thing...

576
45:54.899 --> 45:56.659
You want me to come with you?

577
45:59.323 --> 46:04.140
I don't want to hold you back anymore.

578
46:04.140 --> 46:06.117
I can walk on my own now.

579
46:06.117 --> 46:09.762
So don't worry and go live your own life.

580
46:09.762 --> 46:11.550
Hold me back?

581
46:11.550 --> 46:14.982
You spent your whole life for me. Why are you telling me to live my own life now?

582
46:15.964 --> 46:20.685
Can't you just do what I ask, just this once?

583
46:45.998 --> 46:48.353
[Seven years ago] Mom, please!

584
46:48.353 --> 46:54.159
I should never have married your father. And I shouldn't have had you.

585
47:31.657 --> 47:33.443
Dad, don't worry.

586
47:35.502 --> 47:36.902
I'll...

587
47:38.542 --> 47:41.925
I'll pass the bar exam. I promise.

588
47:41.925 --> 47:45.629
- We'll make it, all right? - Okay.

589
47:47.409 --> 47:52.702
I'll do anything for you, too, Hye Seong.

590
47:52.702 --> 47:54.102
I'm sorry.

591
48:05.866 --> 48:08.720
- Are you okay? - Yeah, I'm fine.

592
48:16.112 --> 48:20.192
Dad, you must be sick of hospital food. I'll make you something nice. What do you want?

593
48:21.048 --> 48:23.555
- Kimchi stew. - Kimchi stew? Okay.

594
48:39.703 --> 48:43.551
All right. We'll look for another attorney then.

595
49:07.460 --> 49:09.231
He's so stubborn.

596
49:09.231 --> 49:13.162
[Hyeseong's Bunsik]

597
49:17.896 --> 49:21.351
[Thank you for supporting Hyeseong's Bunsik over the years.]

598
49:29.868 --> 49:33.511
Hey, Dad. What's that?

599
49:35.077 --> 49:40.168
I thought maybe Hyeseong's Bunsik could move to Seoul with its owner.

600
49:42.209 --> 49:47.191
Dad, you're not holding me back. You're my whole world. You know that?

601
49:47.191 --> 49:48.966
Don't ever say that again.

602
49:48.966 --> 49:53.069
If you left me here in Gwangjin, you'd keep thinking about me, right?

603
49:53.069 --> 49:55.699
Of course! I'd think about you every day!

604
49:57.202 --> 50:01.583
That's what holding you back means. I'd be making you worry about me.

605
50:02.197 --> 50:05.672
So I've decided. I'm going with you.

606
50:07.570 --> 50:09.573
Thanks, Dad.

607
50:09.573 --> 50:10.973
You don't have to thank me.

608
50:12.200 --> 50:14.240
- Is this all? - Yeah.

609
50:20.125 --> 50:23.517
Make sure you leave the house. It's dangerous.

610
50:44.691 --> 50:47.323
What are you doing here?

611
50:56.954 --> 51:00.194
Min Kyung! You...

612
51:48.235 --> 51:50.738
I'm terrified.

613
51:52.054 --> 51:55.637
I don't care about the two billion won. I can't do this anymore.

614
51:55.637 --> 51:57.551
I'm calling the police right now.

615
51:57.551 --> 51:59.117
Wait.

616
51:59.117 --> 52:00.517
Just a moment.

617
52:05.689 --> 52:09.256
Let's try this one last time. We can still call the police afterward.

618
52:11.194 --> 52:13.284
[Complaint: Kim Min Kyung and Ma Jeong Jin shall be divorced]

619
52:16.113 --> 52:17.294
[Defendant's Drug Use and Coercion of Others]

620
52:17.294 --> 52:18.368
[Video Stills of the Defendant Using Drugs]

621
52:18.368 --> 52:19.394
[Defendant's Drugs and Syringes]

622
52:22.327 --> 52:26.667
You said we had to keep this confidential. Why did you write up a complaint?

623
52:26.667 --> 52:30.866
There's no rule saying a complaint can only be filed with the court.

624
52:30.866 --> 52:34.566
There's nothing to hear! Let's go to trial!

625
52:37.439 --> 52:38.523
[Defendant's table]

626
52:38.523 --> 52:42.313
Since his lawyer isn't helping us reach a settlement, let's send it directly to him.

627
52:45.937 --> 52:48.164
Stay at a hotel for just three days.

628
52:49.183 --> 52:53.398
You called me this late because you had nowhere else to go, right?

629
52:57.711 --> 52:59.855
Oh, I can't accept this.

630
53:03.698 --> 53:06.685
I'll deduct it from the success fee later.

631
53:06.685 --> 53:12.551
Go enjoy a little staycation. Swim, have a nice breakfast.

632
53:13.337 --> 53:16.478
All the things you missed out on while spending five years cleaning the house.

633
53:19.176 --> 53:22.291
And if he calls, don't answer.

634
53:22.291 --> 53:25.459
It's his turn to live in fear now.

635
53:26.255 --> 53:29.990
We're close to reaching a settlement.

636
53:49.456 --> 53:53.775
[Complaint: Kim Min Kyung and Ma Jeong Jin shall be divorced]

637
53:55.757 --> 53:57.157
What's this?

638
53:58.845 --> 54:01.449
Oh, come on. What a joke.

639
54:28.475 --> 54:30.735
Beautiful.

640
54:32.347 --> 54:37.472
I forgot how beautiful this city is at night.

641
54:59.524 --> 55:00.816
[Ma Jeong Jin] Hey, did you go file a complaint?

642
55:00.816 --> 55:03.897
Don't even think about it! Are you saying you won't settle?

643
55:03.897 --> 55:04.988
We need to talk.

644
55:04.988 --> 55:07.916
Why aren't you answering my calls? You think I'm kidding?

645
55:33.939 --> 55:35.002
[REBOM Law Firm]

646
55:42.145 --> 55:43.150
[TAESU Law Firm]

647
55:50.717 --> 55:52.999
I'm sorry, Attorney Park.

648
55:55.264 --> 55:59.756
Don't be. Congratulations. I'll see you around.

649
55:59.756 --> 56:01.356
Okay.

650
56:14.359 --> 56:15.759
Come this way.

651
56:25.295 --> 56:28.981
[Korea Legal Culture Foundation Award Attorney Cha Eun Kyung]

652
56:37.161 --> 56:39.713
[Power Woman of the Year Cha Eun Kyung]

653
56:49.052 --> 56:53.791
You'll join me for three consultations and court appearances a week.

654
56:53.791 --> 56:55.006
Is that okay?

655
56:55.006 --> 56:57.202
Yes! That sounds great!

656
56:57.202 --> 57:00.409
I've never had that opportunity at my old firm.

657
57:03.077 --> 57:06.697
It's just orientation today, so take a look around and get settled.

658
57:06.697 --> 57:09.443
I'll give you your first assignments on your first official day.

659
57:10.550 --> 57:11.950
Yes.

660
57:13.017 --> 57:18.595
Could I look through some case files first?

661
57:19.748 --> 57:23.398
I don't have much experience with divorce cases, so I'd like to read up on them.

662
57:24.675 --> 57:26.075
Sure.

663
57:26.666 --> 57:28.486
[Senior Partner Cha Eun Kyung]

664
57:31.640 --> 57:32.847
Here you go.

665
57:32.847 --> 57:34.342
Thank you.

666
57:40.649 --> 57:44.106
Is this... drugs?

667
57:44.106 --> 57:46.394
Have you never seen a drug case before?

668
57:46.394 --> 57:49.116
No. This is my first one!

669
57:49.116 --> 57:50.284
Is it a criminal case?

670
57:50.284 --> 57:52.745
No, it's the other party in the divorce case.

671
57:52.745 --> 57:57.125
We've already made a deal that we won't report him for now.

672
57:57.974 --> 58:00.370
That's definitely worth using in the negotiation.

673
58:00.370 --> 58:03.608
If we report his drug use, he'll be in serious trouble.

674
58:03.608 --> 58:05.136
He'd certainly be arrested.

675
58:05.136 --> 58:09.909
And everyone involved would be prosecuted. So the others would blame him, too.

676
58:11.127 --> 58:13.905
You seem to know a lot about criminal cases.

677
58:13.905 --> 58:15.430
Exactly.

678
58:15.430 --> 58:19.563
I'm waiting for the fear of being reported to make him pay two billion won.

679
58:19.563 --> 58:21.532
Two billion won?

680
58:22.149 --> 58:23.688
Is that even possible?

681
58:23.688 --> 58:25.267
Why not?

682
58:25.267 --> 58:27.517
That's the price of keeping him out of prison.

683
58:28.738 --> 58:30.424
Like I told you,

684
58:30.424 --> 58:34.689
you have to chase down every little lead in a divorce case.

685
58:40.789 --> 58:44.712
You're not like the others.

686
58:44.712 --> 58:45.745
Me?

687
58:45.745 --> 58:49.139
"We should report drug offenders in the public interest."

688
58:49.139 --> 58:53.134
"We should put society's interests ahead of our own."

689
58:53.134 --> 58:55.223
You don't say things like that.

690
58:55.223 --> 58:57.184
I've been a lawyer for five years.

691
58:57.184 --> 59:02.443
I've learned to separate my role as a lawyer from my personal morals.

692
59:03.770 --> 59:08.103
Personally, I'd like to file criminal complaints for assault and drug use right away.

693
59:12.170 --> 59:14.172
Speaking of that...

694
59:14.172 --> 59:17.173
Do you remember the difference between a complaint and a report?

695
59:17.173 --> 59:19.404
You learned that in law school.

696
59:19.404 --> 59:22.112
Yes. A complaint is filed by the victim,

697
59:22.112 --> 59:27.317
while a report can be filed by a third party.

698
59:27.317 --> 59:28.909
Why are you asking me?

699
59:28.909 --> 59:31.587
Just testing your memory.

700
59:33.522 --> 59:34.922
Yes.

701
59:36.003 --> 59:40.337
Attorney Cha, Ms. Kim's husband is calling. Should I put him through?

702
59:41.933 --> 59:44.665
Let's make him sweat a little.

703
59:44.665 --> 59:47.452
Tell him I'm in court and will call back.

704
59:47.452 --> 59:48.852
Yes.

705
01:00:12.819 --> 01:00:15.239
- Hello. - The apartment is now in her name.

706
01:00:15.239 --> 01:00:19.747
I still can't believe you gave away two billion won. I've never seen anything like it.

707
01:00:19.747 --> 01:00:23.558
It's better than going to prison!

708
01:00:25.109 --> 01:00:26.896
What the...

709
01:00:30.235 --> 01:00:32.883
Kim Min Kyung... You thief!

710
01:00:52.215 --> 01:00:53.933
Are you Ma Jeong Jin?

711
01:00:56.131 --> 01:00:57.531
Yes, I am.

712
01:01:02.184 --> 01:01:05.395
- You're under arrest on drug charges. - Let go!

713
01:01:05.395 --> 01:01:07.230
Don't move!

714
01:01:07.230 --> 01:01:10.025
You have the right to an attorney and the right to remain silent.

715
01:01:10.025 --> 01:01:13.652
Anything you say can be used against you in court.

716
01:01:19.313 --> 01:01:20.713
Hello?

717
01:01:21.433 --> 01:01:23.622
Did Ma Jeong Jin get arrested by the police?

718
01:01:23.622 --> 01:01:27.806
Yes. The police called me. Was it you?

719
01:01:27.806 --> 01:01:31.630
No. A deal is a deal.

720
01:01:33.465 --> 01:01:36.339
He must have a lot of enemies.

721
01:01:36.339 --> 01:01:39.624
His drug buddies turned on him.

722
01:01:39.624 --> 01:01:41.370
What goes around comes around.

723
01:01:42.424 --> 01:01:46.947
Ms. Kim, you can go home now.

724
01:01:46.947 --> 01:01:49.395
Back to your safe home.

725
01:01:51.734 --> 01:01:54.021
Thank you, Attorney Cha.

726
01:01:54.917 --> 01:01:56.717
Thank you so much.

727
01:02:02.492 --> 01:02:06.611
Do you remember the difference between a complaint and a report?

728
01:02:06.611 --> 01:02:09.342
Yes. A complaint is filed by the victim,

729
01:02:09.342 --> 01:02:14.502
while a report can be filed by a third party.

730
01:02:14.502 --> 01:02:16.198
Why are you asking me?

731
01:02:16.198 --> 01:02:17.801
Just testing your memory.

732
01:02:17.801 --> 01:02:20.127
She got what I was getting at?

733
01:02:25.805 --> 01:02:26.855
Yes, Ma'am.

734
01:02:26.855 --> 01:02:29.517
Ma Jeong Jin has been arrested.

735
01:02:29.517 --> 01:02:32.036
Oh, really?

736
01:02:32.036 --> 01:02:34.943
Looks like a third party reported him.

737
01:02:34.943 --> 01:02:39.986
I'll officially be part of REBOM starting next week, as stated in my contract.

738
01:02:39.986 --> 01:02:41.419
So I'm still a third party for now!

739
01:02:41.419 --> 01:02:43.899
How did you figure that out so quickly?

740
01:02:44.928 --> 01:02:46.583
You can tell you're experienced.

741
01:02:47.331 --> 01:02:49.958
I've already learned so much on my first day!

742
01:02:49.958 --> 01:02:51.209
Good work.

743
01:02:51.209 --> 01:02:52.318
Thank you.

744
01:02:57.758 --> 01:02:59.257
Can I...

745
01:03:00.743 --> 01:03:04.543
ask why you chose REBOM?

746
01:03:08.117 --> 01:03:12.542
I'm actually really into divorce cases.

747
01:03:12.542 --> 01:03:17.319
My dream is to become a registered divorce specialist, just like you.

748
01:03:17.319 --> 01:03:18.918
I see.

749
01:03:19.831 --> 01:03:21.749
I was worried for nothing.

750
01:03:23.331 --> 01:03:26.773
You'll learn all about divorce cases at REBOM.

751
01:03:26.773 --> 01:03:27.903
Get ready.

752
01:03:28.961 --> 01:03:30.361
I will!

753
01:03:36.394 --> 01:03:39.617
Get home safe.

754
01:03:39.617 --> 01:03:41.417
- Take care. - You too.

755
01:03:45.484 --> 01:03:46.884
Hye Seong!

756
01:04:06.720 --> 01:04:12.392
Wow, look at you! Looking pretty good in Seoul.

757
01:04:15.127 --> 01:04:17.842
And you got a job at such a fancy firm.

758
01:04:26.726 --> 01:04:30.367
Can I ask why you chose REBOM?

759
01:04:35.939 --> 01:04:37.934
If I team up with you,

760
01:04:40.388 --> 01:04:43.643
I think I can get this woman out of my dad's life.

761
01:05:36.345 --> 01:05:39.211
How did you find out about your husband's affair?

762
01:05:39.211 --> 01:05:41.258
I guess it wasn't just physical. He had feelings for her, too.

763
01:05:41.258 --> 01:05:43.582
That upsets me. I don't want to hire your firm anymore!

764
01:05:43.582 --> 01:05:45.950
If I feature the person everyone's talking about right on my channel,

765
01:05:45.950 --> 01:05:48.428
the algorithm will pick it up, and my subscribers will double!

766
01:05:48.428 --> 01:05:53.663
Attorney Kang, you'll have to let go of a lot of your old ways.
